  "limitations": [
    "All newly extracted references require emulator replay validation before oracle use. Hash agreement does not establish unique completion evidence.",
    "Task generation and parity still use the pinned upstream checkpoints; this plan does not replace scoring.",
    "Dev milestones are selected adapter-defined intermediates and completion references, not an official exhaustive level list.",
    "The three unreleased secret test games cannot be reconstructed from the public repository.",
    "The Mario ending reconstruction differs from the published palette and exceeds its threshold. The Incredible Machine final reconstruction also exceeds its threshold. Original published references are preserved for comparison.",
    "Remastered and source-port visuals are accepted as walkthrough sources but may not match original-emulator frames.",
    "X-COM sources use OpenXcom and include an overlapping webcam; clean emulator captures are needed. Only the Cydonia assault and final victory milestones are currently extracted from the 76-part playlist.",
    "Age of Empires includes Rise of Rome and additional campaigns. Its 61 source-verified victory screens use generic sequence labels; OCR mission names are evidence, not canonical IDs. One earlier screen collides with the final reference.",
    "Doom includes Ultimate Doom episode 4; Donkey Kong includes optional Lost World content; Quake milestones cover levels visited in this walkthrough, not every possible secret level.",
    "Video length and elapsed fractions are proxies for walkthrough length, not expected play time, checkpoint score weights, or replay execution time. X-COM playlist and individual-video metadata durations differ slightly.",
    "Generated PNGs, gallery, and full pairwise report are external artifacts; source plans, provenance, and this summary are versioned."
